# Local continuation markers.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY'S CHOICE, not a rule the skill imposes. `write-continue-here`'s lifecycle step
# states the tracked-vs-ignored trade-off and deliberately enforces neither (#775); an earlier
# edition told every consumer to add this line, which ruled out the tracked lifecycle its own
# complement supports. We ignore because handoffs here are scratch between two sessions and we
# do not want their churn in the history — the cost being that consuming one is final, so an
# edition worth keeping goes to the PARENT-level archive at ../misc/handoff-archive/<date>/
# BEFORE it is deleted — that path is outside this repository, and read repo-relative it
# resolves to nothing.
#
# The glob, not the bare name: the skill drafts to CONTINUE_HERE.draft.md and renames it only
# after the verification round, so the bare name left every draft untracked-but-visible — and a
# draft is the one edition most likely to be swept into an unrelated commit by a `git add -A`.
CONTINUE_HERE*.md

# Campfire state (local, not shared)
.agent-almanac/

# Universal adapter install target (created by CLI tests)
.agents/

# Adapter broken-symlink audit fixture (created by CLI tests)
.tmp-test-audit/

# Node dependencies
node_modules/

# Viz build artifacts
viz/dist/
viz/logs/
viz/.icon-cache.json

# Peon-ping assets
.peon-ping-icon.png
.peon-toast.xml
peon-ping-sound.wav

# Quarto render artifacts
tests/results/**/*.html
*.knit.md

# Rust CLI build cache (the Rust port's source lives on the rust-cli branch, not main)
cli-rs/target/

# Local Claude Code config (not shared)
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
__pycache__/

# Local secrets. `.env` holds API keys used while authoring content that documents a
# third-party service (currently TYPESAFE_API_KEY); nothing in this repository's code or
# gates reads it, and nothing ever should — a gate that needs a key cannot run for a
# contributor who has none.
#
# The glob as well as the bare name, because `.env` alone does not match `.env.local` or
# `.env.production`, and the negation because `.env.example` is the tracked template that
# tells a contributor which names exist without ever carrying a value.
#
# Verify a new variant is actually covered before writing a secret into it:
#   git check-ignore -v .env
# An unignored `.env` is one `git add -A` away from a published credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
